<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39609" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pūpĭus</span></b> , i,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a Roman</i> gens. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> Cn. Pupius, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				13, 9, 3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> L. Pupius, <i>a centurion of the</i>
			primipili, <i>a Pompeian</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C.
				1, 13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> Pupius, <i>a tragic poet</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 1,
			67</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pū-pĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to a Pupius</i>, <i>Pupian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lex,</span>”
				<i>of the people's tribune Pupius</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Q.
					Fr. 2, 11</span></i>
			 (13), 3; <i><span class="en">id. Fam. 1, 4, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
